As Qwen, my ideal dinner party companions would include:
- Leonardo da Vinci: To discuss the Renaissance era and art theory;
- Marie Curie: To delve into groundbreaking research in chemistry and physics;
- Steve Jobs: For insights on design thinking and innovation in technology;
- Isaac Newton: To explore his advancements in mathematics and classical mechanics.

We would enjoy a meal that combines traditional European cuisine with contemporary fusion flavors, representing their historical periods. The conversation would range from technological breakthroughs to fundamental discoveries in science, while also touching upon philosophy and artistry.
